","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"41…Bxe2! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Takes the bishop on e2.","The next best move, 41…d3, would drop Black's winning chances from 92% to 79% (−3.56).","41…Bxe2 trades bishops.","Trades bishops: trading pieces when ahead brings the win closer.","The bishop on e2 can be taken by the king.","White answers 42.Kxe2, taking back."]}],"opening":{"name":"Queen's Gambit Declined: Ragozin Defense, Vienna Variation","eco":"D39","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 13.h4: 25 moves in all, 13 by White and 12 by Black.","Theory runs out after 13.h4: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}